mit 2023)' requirement is not met.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer A names MikeWang as the top author of version7.go with 81.6%, which is correct. It credits Mei Chen with 9.7% and the Time7 accessor. It shows Ravi Menon with only 1.9% and doesn't credit Mei's lines to Ravi. This matches the criterion.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A follows database_sql.go and names Justin Overfelt as the top author with 39.6%, which is in range. It says Ravi's rename left him 0 surviving lines. It says no one holding SQL lines has committed recently. It doesn't name Andrew Stone, David Wheeler or Daniel Souza as the other original authors. It names Paul Borman instead. The core of the criterion is met, so I pass it.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A reports only 4.3% of lines held by active people (so about 95.7% owned by departed people), which is correct. But it lists Alexander Rowe and Alex Rowe as separate. It also says 4 people are active rather than naming Ravi, Alex and Kofi. It recommends Mei Chen as an active holder, which is wrong because she left. Several parts of the criterion fail.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A doesn't name Noor Haddad or Sam Okafor as owners. It doesn't count the bots as people. It doesn't say Kofi Mensah has been inactive since 1970. It doesn't address Kofi explicitly, though. It is roughly clean on the noise criterion, so I pass it.\", \"pass\": true}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B says Paul Borman wrote time.go but last committed in 2021. That is wrong, because the real date is 2023. It gives no line share. It lists Sam Okafor as the last committer, and it never credits Paul with the majority of lines. The criterion is not met.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B uses commit-based analysis only. It recommends Ravi Menon as the newest maintainer of version7.go. It gives no line shares and doesn't credit Mei Chen with the Time7 accessor. It names MikeWang as the author of the v7 monotonicity logic. Mei Chen is missing, so it fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B uses --follow to trace database_sql.go back through the rename, which is right. It names David E. Wheeler, Justin Overfelt and Andrew Stone as the original authors, last active 2016-2017. But it recommends Ravi Menon as the SQL reviewer, and it gives no line shares or largest author. It doesn't name Justin Overfelt as the largest author. It doesn't treat Ravi as the author, but it does recommend him as the maintainer. This is borderline, and I fail it because the key largest-author requirement is missing.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B claims nobody has committed in the last 90 days. That contradicts the real active status of Ravi, Alex Rowe and Kofi. It gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It lists Alexander Rowe separately from Alex Rowe, although it hedges. The criterion is not met.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B lists Sam Okafor's activity as a line-ending normalization commit and doesn't call him an owner. It doesn't name Noor Haddad. But it lists Sam Okafor among the relevant people, and it never discusses Kofi Mensah. It also uses 'last commit in repo' for time.go as Sam's line-ending commit, which is a bit sloppy but not ownership. It's borderline. It doesn't name anyone as owner wrongly, so I pass it.\", \"pass\": true}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C names Paul Borman as having the most lines in time.go, but gives no percentage. It says his last commit was in 2016, not 2023, so it is wrong on the date. It lists Sam Okafor with about 18 lines, even though it recognizes that this comes from the line-ending commit. It says Paul is unlikely to be active. The last-commit date is wrong and there is no percentage, so it fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C names MikeWang as the top author of version7.go. It credits Mei Chen with 11 lines and the Time7 accessor, and gives Ravi Menon only 2 lines. It gives no percentages, but the line counts are right. The criterion is mostly met, so I pass it.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C follows database_sql.go and names Justin Overfelt as the main author, with Andrew Stone and David Wheeler as other authors. It says these are 2015-2017 authors with no commits since. It doesn't name Ravi as the author. It gives no percentage, but it meets the main parts.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C says it cannot confirm who is still around. It calls Ravi active, but says Mei and Alexander have been quiet for months. It gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It doesn't name Kofi. It never says the active people hold almost none of the code. The criterion is not met.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C lists Sam Okafor in the time.go table with about 18 lines of 'main authors'. It does note the line-ending issue, but it still counts him as a main author with an 18-line share. It lists Sam among the main authors of time.go in the first table, which counts as naming him an owner. It also doesn't address Kofi, which is a lesser point. It fails on Sam.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":15421,"type":"result","duration_ms":15442,"uuid":"352df9f8-0e98-4d24-bed3-e50cacf1f179","ttft_stream_ms":1939,"time_to_request_ms":570,"first_content_frame_ms":1940,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
